      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "Async onSave breaks the synchronous dispatch caller",
      "description": "onSave now returns a Promise, but dispatch in src/router.js:7 returns it unchanged. The handler in src/main.js:9 then passes that Promise straight to res.end. Node's res.end throws a TypeError for a Promise argument, so every POST /save request crashes the server. A failed writeFile rejection also goes unhandled, and newer Node versions terminate the process on it. Make dispatch and the request handler await the result. Add a catch that answers with an error status.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "onSave now returns a Promise, but dispatch in src/router.js:7 returns it unchanged. The handler in src/main.js:9 then passes that Promise straight to res.end.",
      "consequence": "Node's res.end throws a TypeError for a Promise argument, so every POST /save request crashes the server. A failed writeFile rejection also goes unhandled, and newer Node versions terminate the process on it.",
      "fix": "Make dispatch and the request handler await the result. Add a catch that answers with an error status."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 8,
      "line_end": 8,
      "title": "New snapshot write has no covering test",
      "description": "onSave now writes a file and returns a Promise. No test covers this new behaviour. A test that saved once through the router would have caught the crash. Without tests, later regressions in saving will also go unnoticed. Add a test that saves an id through dispatch. It should check the response text and the contents of the snapshot file.",
